The shopkeeper nods and takes the small shirt.
He searches in the pile of clothes.
Then he gives me another shirt.
He says, "Madam, this shirt is bigger than that one."
"Please try this on."
I take the new shirt.
Today I do not go to the fitting room.
There is a large mirror near the wall of the shop.
I walk towards the mirror.
I put this new shirt on right over my t-shirt.
This is a simple way to test the shirt.
I look at myself in the mirror.
This shirt is longer than the old shirt.
Its shoulder area is also wider.
I move my arms to test the fit.
Now I do not feel any discomfort.
Its fit is much better than the previous shirt.
